{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792872017,"nonce":"fDJWiHq2CqUy2XomoE5VDgcijoo=","title":"CSS opacity cache patching flattens ungrouped overlapping children","message":"Scoped continuation of e0a7502e3e9d71bb983572df7db0033a67da1c48262e53368ae2399bc22e583a and the native walker grouping fix 35b36bb6519ef5dd6847804ac47295f7e6f82638. A non-promoted CSS frame painted at opacity one can have no group command. apply_css_deltas currently multiplies every primitive alpha when opacity changes, losing isolation between overlapping children. It also rejects recovery from zero even when a valid group owns the cached full-opacity children.\n\nRequire a valid group Push before patching a changed CSS opacity. Reject missing/stale command ownership before modifying cache geometry, other records or baselines; let the existing full-paint path establish a group. Patch represented group opacity directly, including zero recovery. Cover keyframe/transition reads and animation precedence, non-promoted public compositor frames from opaque through zero, and malformed metadata cache preservation. Keep promotion policy, independent streams and broader cache ownership as parent scope. Scope checks to touched paths/direct controls, CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2, no push.","files":null}]}